<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:lang="en">
<teiHeader>
<fileDesc>
<titleStmt>
<title>Gloss: TEI customisation for the dataset of sources quoted, adapted,
echoed and alluded to in J. H. Prynne's Poems</title>
<author>Louis Goddard</author>
</titleStmt>
<publicationStmt>
<publisher>Louis Goddard</publisher>
<availability status="free"><licence
target="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</licence>
</availability>
</publicationStmt>
<sourceDesc><p>Written for the gloss dataset (release/gloss.xml).</p>
</sourceDesc>
</fileDesc>
</teiHeader>
<text>
<body>
<head>The Gloss dataset: a TEI customisation</head>

<p>The dataset <ident>release/gloss.xml</ident> records the quotations,
adaptations, echoes and allusions found in J. H. Prynne's <title>Poems</title>
(second edition, Bloodaxe Books, 2005) and <title>Force of Circumstance and
Other Poems</title> (1962). Each entry is one <gi>cit</gi>: the words of
Prynne that the entry concerns, a reference to their page and to the lines of
the poem (counted from its first line, a turned-over line counting once), and a
nested <gi>cit</gi> type="source" with the source's words and a pointer to the
edition in which they were seen. The editions are <gi>biblStruct</gi> records
in the <gi>standOff</gi>, each with its identifiers as <gi>idno</gi>.</p>

<p>Only the elements that the dataset uses are allowed, and the attributes
that carry data have closed value lists: the kind of an entry
(<att>type</att> on <gi>cit</gi>), its confidence (<att>cert</att>), the
unit of a reference (<att>unit</att> on <gi>citedRange</gi>), and the kind of
identifier (<att>type</att> on <gi>idno</gi>).</p>

<div>
<head>Structure</head>
<list>
<item><gi>teiHeader</gi>: title, authors and roles, licence (CC BY 4.0
for the structure, identifiers and metadata; the quoted words are quoted
under fair dealing for criticism and quotation), the source editions, the
method in brief, the line-counting rule, and a <gi>taxonomy</gi> of the
entry types.</item>
<item><gi>standOff</gi>: a <gi>listBibl</gi> type="prynne" of Prynne's
books (each collection with its first publication), and a
<gi>listBibl</gi> type="sources" of the editions quoted.</item>
<item><gi>text</gi>: one <gi>div</gi> type="collection" for each of
Prynne's collections, holding its entries. (<gi>cit</gi> is not allowed in
<gi>standOff</gi> by TEI P5, so the entries are the text of the
dataset.)</item>
</list>
</div>

<div>
<head>An entry</head>
<egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
<cit type="quotation" cert="high" xml:id="g0001" ana="#quotation">
 <quote corresp="poems-2005.xml#p568.9">Flitting under her<lb/>breath in
 catches, bird on briar</quote>
 <bibl><ptr target="#prynne-2005-blue-slides-at-rest"/>
  <title>Partition blurred caloric engine his spiral transfusion</title>
  <citedRange unit="page" from="568" to="568"/>
  <citedRange unit="line" from="9" to="10"/></bibl>
 <cit type="source">
  <quote>Bryd one brere</quote>
  <bibl><ptr target="#robbins-1955-secular-lyrics"/>
   <citedRange unit="item">147</citedRange></bibl>
 </cit>
</cit>
</egXML>
</div>

<div>
<head>Schema</head>
<schemaSpec ident="gloss" start="TEI" prefix="tei_">
<moduleRef key="tei"/>
<moduleRef key="core" include="p head list item title author editor
 respStmt resp name note date publisher pubPlace bibl biblStruct listBibl
 monogr analytic series imprint biblScope citedRange ptr lb gap
 cit quote relatedItem"/>
<moduleRef key="header" include="teiHeader fileDesc titleStmt
 editionStmt edition publicationStmt sourceDesc availability licence idno
 encodingDesc projectDesc editorialDecl samplingDecl classDecl taxonomy
 category catDesc revisionDesc change"/>
<moduleRef key="textstructure" include="TEI text body div"/>
<moduleRef key="linking" include="standOff"/>
<moduleRef key="tagdocs" include="gi att ident"/>
<moduleRef key="analysis" include="interp"/>
<elementSpec ident="interp" mode="delete" module="analysis"/>

<elementSpec ident="cit" mode="change">
 <attList>
  <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="req">
   <valList type="closed" mode="replace">
    <valItem ident="quotation"><desc>Prynne's words reproduce the
     source's words with little or no change.</desc></valItem>
    <valItem ident="adaptation"><desc>The source's words are altered
     (words changed, added, reordered or cut) but plainly
     recognisable.</desc></valItem>
    <valItem ident="echo"><desc>A shorter or looser verbal
     resemblance.</desc></valItem>
    <valItem ident="allusion"><desc>A reference to a specific source
     with few shared words.</desc></valItem>
    <valItem ident="source"><desc>The nested citation of the source
     itself.</desc></valItem>
   </valList>
  </attDef>
 </attList>
</elementSpec>

<classSpec ident="att.global.responsibility" type="atts" mode="change">
 <attList>
  <attDef ident="cert" mode="change">
   <datatype><dataRef key="teidata.enumerated"/></datatype>
   <valList type="closed" mode="replace">
    <valItem ident="high"/><valItem ident="medium"/><valItem ident="low"/>
   </valList>
  </attDef>
 </attList>
</classSpec>

<elementSpec ident="citedRange" mode="change">
 <attList>
  <attDef ident="unit" mode="change">
   <valList type="closed" mode="replace">
    <valItem ident="page"/><valItem ident="line"><desc>On Prynne's side,
     the line of the poem, counted from its first line.</desc></valItem>
    <valItem ident="title"><desc>Prynne's words are in the title of the
     poem or collection.</desc></valItem>
    <valItem ident="epigraph"/><valItem ident="dedication"/>
    <valItem ident="chapter"/><valItem ident="verse"/>
    <valItem ident="item"/><valItem ident="column"/>
    <valItem ident="section"/><valItem ident="act-scene-line"/>
    <valItem ident="folio"/><valItem ident="stanza"/>
    <valItem ident="book"/><valItem ident="part"/>
    <valItem ident="entry"/><valItem ident="paragraph"/>
    <valItem ident="none"/>
   </valList>
  </attDef>
 </attList>
</elementSpec>

<elementSpec ident="idno" mode="change">
 <attList>
  <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="req">
   <valList type="closed" mode="replace">
    <valItem ident="DOI"/><valItem ident="ISBN"/><valItem ident="OCLC"/>
    <valItem ident="LCCN"/><valItem ident="LCC"/>
    <valItem ident="IA"><desc>Internet Archive item.</desc></valItem>
    <valItem ident="Gutenberg"><desc>Project Gutenberg ebook
     number.</desc></valItem>
    <valItem ident="Wikidata"/><valItem ident="VIAF"/>
    <valItem ident="OSIS"/><valItem ident="CTS"/><valItem ident="URL"/>
   </valList>
  </attDef>
 </attList>
</elementSpec>
</schemaSpec>
</div>
</body>
</text>
</TEI>
